    {
      "id": "claim_6bf0e5d586854d1bada075d927bf64b7",
      "statement": "The README claims the script is 'designed for JPEG images', but the code is broader: process_image gates on SUPPORTED_FORMATS = {'.jpg', '.jpeg', '.png', '.heic', '.tiff', '.tif', '.bmp', '.webp'}, so non-JPEG formats are sorted, dated, and copied. The JPEG-only statement is true only of the metadata-sensitive steps: tagging is strictly JPEG-only by extension check, rotation depends on Pillow's _getexif() (absent for other formats, so they are never rotated), and exifread-based dating falls back to file ctime for formats without readable EXIF.",
